{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I sought the Lord and he [Ab]answered me
[Eb]He delivered me from [Ab]all my fears
[Cm]My [Bb6]soul boasts in the [Abmaj7]Lord today
Let the hum[Eb]ble hear and [Bb]re[Eb]joice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Magnify [Bb]the Lord with [Eb]me
[Ab]Let us exalt [Bb]his name to[Cm]gether
[Ab]I sought the [Bb]Lord and he [Eb]an[Bb/D]swered [Cm]me
De[Ab]livered me from [Bb]all my [Eb]fears [Ab]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Those who look to him [Ab]are radiant
[Eb]Their faces will never [Ab]be ashamed
[Cm]This [Bb]poor man called and the [Ab]Lord heard
He saved [Eb]him out of [Bb]all his trou[Eb]bles
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Magnify [Bb]the Lord with [Eb]me
[Ab]Let us exalt [Bb]his name to[Cm]gether
[Ab]I sought [Bb]the Lord and he [Eb]an[Bb/D]swered [Cm]me
De[Ab]livered me from [Bb]all my [Eb]fears
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The [Ab]angel of the Lord encamps a[Cm]round
[Ab]Those who fear him he res[Eb]cues
His [Ab]praise will always be [Cm]on my lips
I will [Ab]bless the Lord [Bb]at all [Eb]times
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]I sought the [Bb]Lord and he [Eb]an[Bb/D]swered [Cm]me
